f^2 &= d^2.
\end{align*}From the first equation, $f - d = \frac{2}{5}.$  Since $f^2 = d^2,$ $f = d$ or $f = -d.$  We cannot have $f = d,$ so $f = -d.$  Then $2f = \frac{2}{5},$ so $f = \frac{2}{5}.$

